  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0053\" contains 9 tables. The main tables are \"canvas_posts\", \"canvas_tags\", \"canvas_topics\", \"canvas_user_meta\", \"canvas_views\", \"canvas_visits\", and \"users\".\nThe \"canvas_posts\" table represents a collection of blog posts. It has columns for id, slug, title, summary, body, published_at, featured_image, featured_image_caption, user_id, meta, created_at, updated_at, and deleted_at. The user_id column references the id column in the \"users\" table, establishing a foreign key relationship.\nThe \"canvas_posts_tags\" table represents the many-to-many relationship between posts and tags. It has columns for tag_id and post_id, both of which reference the id column in their respective tables. The tag_id references the \"canvas_tags\" table, and the post_id references the \"canvas_posts\" table.\nThe \"canvas_posts_topics\" table represents the many-to-many relationship between posts and topics. It has columns for post_id and topic_id, both of which reference the id column in their respective tables. The post_id references the \"canvas_posts\" table, and the topic_id references the \"canvas_topics\" table.\nThe \"canvas_tags\" table represents a collection of tags. It has columns for id, slug, name, user_id, created_at, updated_at, and deleted_at. The user_id column references the id column in the \"users\" table, establishing a foreign key relationship.\nThe \"canvas_topics\" table represents a collection of topics. It has columns for id, slug, name, user_id, created_at, updated_at, and deleted_at. The user_id column references the id column in the \"users\" table, establishing a foreign key relationship.\nThe \"canvas_user_meta\" table represents additional user metadata. It has columns for id, user_id, username, summary, avatar, dark_mode, digest, locale, created_at, and updated_at. The user_id column references the id column in the \"users\" table, establishing a foreign key relationship.\nThe \"canvas_views\" and \"canvas_visits\" tables represent user interactions with posts. They have columns for id, post_id, ip, agent, referer, created_at, and updated_at. The post_id column references the id column in the \"canvas_posts\" table, establishing a foreign key relationship.\nThe \"users\" table represents a collection of users. It has columns for id, name, email, email_verified_at, password, remember_token, created_at, and updated_at. It is the main table for user authentication and profile information.\nThis schema is designed to maintain a clean and efficient data structure for a blog platform, with tables representing different entities and relationships between them. It ensures referential integrity by using foreign key constraints to maintain the relationships between tables.",
  "gold_question": "Laravel Publishing Platform: Canvas\n\n 1) Background / Context\nCanvas is an open-source blogging package designed to integrate seamlessly into existing Laravel applications. Inspired by Medium, the platform offers a clean, distraction-free writing environment and advanced analytics to help users understand content performance and reader engagement.\n\n 2) Objectives\nThe primary objective of Canvas is to provide a robust and user-friendly blogging platform that can be easily incorporated into a Laravel project. It aims to facilitate content creation, management, and detailed analytics on user interaction.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Administrators: Manage overall platform settings, user roles, and permissions.\n- Editors: Publish and manage posts (including those of other users).\n- Contributors: Create and manage their own posts, without publishing rights.\n- Readers: Access published content and contribute to viewing statistics.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- User Management: \n  - Default admin user setup on installation.\n  - CRUD operations for user profiles and role assignments.\n\n- Content Management:\n  - Create, edit, and delete posts with features like tagging and categorization by topics.\n  - Schedule posts with publishing dates.\n\n- Roles and Permissions:\n  - Three predefined roles: Contributor, Editor, Admin.\n  - Role-specific access for content creation, management, and publication.\n\n- Analytics:\n  - Track monthly trends and reader traffic.\n  - Collect and display post view data based on IP, user agent, and referer.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: The platform should efficiently support typical load usage scenarios consistent with medium-sized blogging environments.\n- Usability: The interface should be intuitive and easy to navigate for all roles.\n- Security: Ensure secure user authentication and data protection, especially regarding publish and view analytics data linkage.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0053.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0053\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email_verified_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `remember_token` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `canvas_posts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `published_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `featured_image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `featured_image_caption` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `meta` json DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `deleted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_posts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `canvas_tags` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `deleted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_tags_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `canvas_topics` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `deleted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_topics_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `canvas_user_meta` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `dark_mode` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `digest` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_user_meta_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `canvas_views` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ip` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `agent` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `referer` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_views_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `canvas_posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `canvas_visits` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ip` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `agent` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `referer` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_visits_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `canvas_posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `canvas_posts_tags` (\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`tag_id`, `post_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_posts_tags_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`tag_id`) REFERENCES `canvas_tags` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_posts_tags_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `canvas_posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `canvas_posts_topics` (\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `topic_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`post_id`, `topic_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_posts_topics_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `canvas_posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `canvas_posts_topics_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`topic_id`) REFERENCES `canvas_topics` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
